      "id": 1,
      "text": "Yorkshire, New York, was carved out of the town of Ischua in 1820, marking its official birth as a separate municipality.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yorkshire%2C_New_York",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Just seven years later, the southern portion split off to create the town of Machias, reshaping Yorkshire’s early borders.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yorkshire%2C_New_York",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town’s northern edge follows Cattaraugus Creek, while its eastern frontier meets Wyoming County, giving Yorkshire a natural boundary feel.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yorkshire%2C_New_York",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "New York State Routes 16 and 39 cross in Yorkshire, briefly sharing a stretch before diverging toward the county’s heart.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yorkshire%2C_New_York",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Delevan, a small village in Yorkshire’s northeast, sits south of the main town center along Route 16 and several county roads.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yorkshire%2C_New_York",
